 <section class="chapter hk-implementation"><div class="chapter-inner"><div class="chapter-index">12 / Implementation</div><div class="lf-split"><h2 class="chapter-title">Zero dependency did not mean <em>zero discipline.</em></h2><div class="lf-copy"><p>The capture route reads raw buffers before middleware can consume or transform them. A promise queue serialises mutations, unique temporary files replace the JSON store atomically, and retention caps each channel at one hundred events.</p><p>Traversal-safe static delivery, body-size limits, response helpers, SSE cleanup and testable router behavior replace the conveniences usually delegated to packages.</p></div></div><div class="hk-runtime"><span>node:http</span><i>ROUTER</i><i>MIDDLEWARE</i><i>RAW BODY</i><i>REDACT</i><i>ATOMIC STORE</i><i>SSE</i><span>BROWSER</span></div></div></section>

